{"full":"openrundev/openrun","name":"openrun","description":"Deployment platform for teams to deploy internal tools. Deploy web apps declaratively, on a single-node or on Kubernetes, with OIDC/SAML auth and RBAC.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":980,"forks":33,"created":"2023-04-13T18:29:51Z","updated":"2026-10-02T21:39:34Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://openrun.dev/","topics":["appserver","containers","deployment","devops-tools","docker","golang","htmx","internal-tools","kubernetes","kubernetes-deployment","openrun","self-hosted","starlark"],"demo":"https://utils.demo.clace.io/console/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T16:49:35.494Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T16:49:35.494Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T16:49:35.494Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:25:46.098Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T21:18:20.145Z","stars":979,"forks":33},{"at":"2026-10-04T08:17:32.217Z","stars":979,"forks":33},{"at":"2026-10-05T16:49:35.494Z","stars":980,"forks":33}],"technologies":["Go"],"overviewAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T05:15:49.141Z","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["OpenRun is an Apache-2.0 licensed open source, self-hosted GitOps platform for deploying web apps and internal tools. Run the single binary on one server with Docker/Podman, or deploy apps onto a Kubernetes cluster with the same declarative config. OpenRun provides declarative GitOps based blue-green deployment, OAuth/OIDC/SAML access controls, RBAC, audit logs, TLS certs and secrets management. Apps are deployed directly from the git repo, no build server required. OpenRun scales idle apps down to zero and supports atomic updates across multiple apps.","This repo hosts the source code for OpenRun. The source for the documentation site openrun.dev is in the docs folder. App specifications, which are templates to create apps, are defined in the appspecs repo. Sample apps are in the apps repo."],"features":["Architecture Overview","Database Service Bindings","SQLite Backups with Litestream","Create and manage apps declaratively, through GitOps","Service bindings to provision isolated Postgres/MySQL/SQLite/Redis database accounts for apps, with more databases supported through binding providers"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/openrundev/openrun/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c101e4aa47c8174f9650c0ea77794adc0814962c9af77bf86bd453c10440ba1c","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T07:02:42.541Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T05:15:55.743Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"OpenRun is an Apache-2.0 licensed open source, self-hosted GitOps platform for deploying web apps and internal tools. Run the single binary on one server with Docker/Podman, or deploy apps onto a Kubernetes cluster with the same declarative config. OpenRun provides declarative GitOps based blue-green deployment, OAuth/OIDC/SAML access controls, RBAC, audit logs, TLS certs and secrets management. Apps are deployed directly from the git repo, no build server required. OpenRun scales idle apps down to zero and supports atomic updates across multiple apps.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/openrundev/openrun/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Features which are built for this use case include: > > - Declarative Config: Manage apps declaratively in git, allowing teams to follow regular SDLC for config > - OAuth/OIDC/SAML with RBAC: Manage who can access which app using RBAC > - Service Bindings: Configure a database once and safely provision it across apps, each app getting its own isolated account > - Audit Logs:…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/openrundev/openrun/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"c101e4aa47c8174f9650c0ea77794adc0814962c9af77bf86bd453c10440ba1c","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/openrundev/openrun/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T05:15:55.743Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-02T21:39:34Z","d